{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Mathlib.ExtensionClass","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Mathlib.ExtensionClass","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.SelfDualSES","lean:module:Mathlib.RingTheory.SimpleModule.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.LinearAlgebra.Projection","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":24,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.ExtensionClass.heckeSES_isSplit_of_ordered","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.ExtensionClass.heckeSES_isSplit_of_ordered","kind":"theorem","line":442,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/ExtensionClass.lean#L442-L455","doc":"**The sym/asym sequence splits at every real substrate value.**\n\nNot only at `q₀ ≈ 1.1099`, and not only away from roots of unity: at\n*every* nonzero `q` in an ordered field. This is the archimedean form of\nthe refutation, and it is the reason the withdrawn claim cannot be rescued\nby moving it to a degenerate `q` — in this normalisation there is no real\ndegenerate `q` to move it to. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.ExtensionClass.twoQ_ne_zero_of_ordered","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.ExtensionClass.twoQ_ne_zero_of_ordered","kind":"theorem","line":429,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/ExtensionClass.lean#L429-L440","doc":"**The gap never vanishes over an ordered field.** `q² + 1 ≥ 1 > 0`.\n\nSo the collision locus of the corpus's normalisation is not reached by any\nreal substrate value — root of unity or not. Relocating a non-split\nextension to a degenerate `q` is therefore unavailable on the archimedean\nside of the §7c wall, where `phase-transition-boundary` lives. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.ExtensionClass.twoQ_eq_zero_iff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.ExtensionClass.twoQ_eq_zero_iff","kind":"theorem","line":406,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/ExtensionClass.lean#L406-L427","doc":"**`[2]_q = q + q⁻¹` vanishes exactly on `q² + 1 = 0`.**\n\nThe inverse is carried as a hypothesis `q * u = 1` rather than written\n`q⁻¹`, because `R_q = ℤ[q, q⁻¹]` is a ring with no `Inv` instance even\nthough `q` is invertible in it (`QOU.GroundRing`).\n\nIn the corpus's normalisation `(σ − q)(σ + q⁻¹) = 0`\n(`rem:hecke-algebra-from-braiding`) the eigenvalue difference is\n`q − (−q⁻¹) = q + q⁻¹`, so this is the locus where the symmetric and\nantisymmetric channels collide — `q = ±i`, not `q = −1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.ExtensionClass.heckeSES_isSplit","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.ExtensionClass.heckeSES_isSplit","kind":"theorem","line":380,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/ExtensionClass.lean#L380-L395","doc":"**The sym/asym sequence splits.**\n\nThis is the refutation of `0 → V_sym → V_mixed → V_asym → 0` being\nnon-split, stated over the weakest hypothesis that suffices: the Hecke\nquadratic and `[2]_q` invertible. It does not go through semisimplicity, so\nit survives even a reader who rejects `prop:knot-eigenbasis-complete`(1). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.ExtensionClass.heckeSES","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.ExtensionClass.heckeSES","kind":"def","line":367,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/ExtensionClass.lean#L367-L378","doc":"The eigenspace sequence of a Hecke generator, as an `SES`:\n`0 → ker(σ − q) → M → M ⧸ ker(σ − q) → 0`. Exactness is free, exactly as for\n`selfDualSES`; writing the sequence down proves nothing. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.ExtensionClass.isCompl_ker_quadratic","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.ExtensionClass.isCompl_ker_quadratic","kind":"theorem","line":302,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/ExtensionClass.lean#L302-L365","doc":"**A quadratic with invertible eigenvalue gap splits its eigenspaces.**\n\nWith `a = q` and `b = q⁻¹` this is the Hecke relation, and `a + b = [2]_q`.\nThe splitting is explicit: `x = u·(f x + b·x) + u·(a·x − f x)` for\n`u = [2]_q⁻¹`, the first summand killed by `f − a` and the second by\n`f + b`. Nothing else is used, so the conclusion holds over any commutative\nring in which `[2]_q` is invertible — in particular over `ℝ` at every\n`q₀ > 0`, and over `ℤ[q, q⁻¹]` it does not, which is the only place the\nquestion could still have been open. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.ExtensionClass.selfDual_isSplit","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.ExtensionClass.selfDual_isSplit","kind":"theorem","line":268,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/ExtensionClass.lean#L268-L292","doc":"**The self-duality sequence splits, so it has no extension class.**\n\nGiven `2` invertible and no 2-torsion, `Ω⁺` is a complement to `Ω⁻`\n(`isCompl_plus_minus`), and the quotient map restricted to it is the\nsection.\n\nRead together with the module docstring: this says the topological charge\ndoes **not** live in the `⋆_q` decomposition. And it does not even say that\nover the ground ring — `2` is not invertible in `R_q = ℤ[q, q⁻¹]`, so the\nhypothesis fails there and the sequence is not known to split at all. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.ExtensionClass.selfDualSES","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.ExtensionClass.selfDualSES","kind":"def","line":257,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/ExtensionClass.lean#L257-L266","doc":"The eigenspace sequence of an involution, as an `SES`:\n`0 → Ω⁻ → Ω² → Ω²/Ω⁻ → 0`. Exactness is free (`minus_ses_exact`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.ExtensionClass.isSplit_of_isSemisimpleRing","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.ExtensionClass.isSplit_of_isSemisimpleRing","kind":"theorem","line":243,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/ExtensionClass.lean#L243-L251","doc":"**Over a semisimple algebra there are no non-split extensions at all.**\n\nThis is what `Ext¹_{H_n(q)}(V_asym, V_sym) ≅ ℤ` runs into.\n`prop:knot-eigenbasis-complete`(1) makes `H_n(q₀) ≅ ℂ[S_n]` semisimple at\nthe substrate (Jimbo, `q₀` not a root of unity), and then **no** pair of\n`H_n(q₀)`-modules admits a non-split extension — not the sym/asym pair and\nnot any other. There is no group to be `ℤ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.ExtensionClass.isSplit_of_isSemisimpleModule","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.ExtensionClass.isSplit_of_isSemisimpleModule","kind":"theorem","line":234,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/ExtensionClass.lean#L234-L241","doc":"**Every short exact sequence with semisimple middle term splits.**\n\nSemisimplicity is exactly the statement that every submodule is a direct\nsummand, so `ker proj` has a complement and `isSplit_of_isCompl` applies. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.ExtensionClass.isSplit_of_isCompl","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.ExtensionClass.isSplit_of_isCompl","kind":"theorem","line":193,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/ExtensionClass.lean#L193-L228","doc":"**A direct-summand decomposition splits the sequence** — the converse of\n`isCompl_of_isSplit`.\n\nGiven a complement `p` to `range incl = ker proj`, the projection restricted\nto `p` is a bijection onto `A`: injective because `p` meets `ker proj`\ntrivially, surjective because every `b` is a sum of something in `ker proj`\nand something in `p`. Its inverse, followed by the inclusion of `p`, is the\nsection. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.ExtensionClass.isCompl_of_isSplit","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.ExtensionClass.isCompl_of_isSplit","kind":"theorem","line":165,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/ExtensionClass.lean#L165-L191","doc":"**A split sequence is a direct sum**, so it carries no extension data.\n\nThis is why \"the charge is the failure to split\" is the right reading: a\nsplit sequence is determined by its ends, and there is nothing left for a\nclass in `Ext¹` to record. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.ExtensionClass.IsSplit","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.ExtensionClass.IsSplit","kind":"def","line":162,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/ExtensionClass.lean#L162-L163","doc":"The sequence splits. Unambiguous by the splitting lemma above. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.ExtensionClass.hasRetraction_of_hasSection","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.ExtensionClass.hasRetraction_of_hasSection","kind":"theorem","line":130,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/ExtensionClass.lean#L130-L160","doc":"**The splitting lemma**, right to left.\n\nA section `s` makes `b - s (proj b)` land in `ker proj = range incl`, and\n`incl` is injective, so that element has a unique preimage in `C`. The\nretraction sends `b` there. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.ExtensionClass.HasRetraction","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.ExtensionClass.HasRetraction","kind":"def","line":127,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/ExtensionClass.lean#L127-L128","doc":"**Left splitting**: the inclusion admits a retraction. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.ExtensionClass.HasSection","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.ExtensionClass.HasSection","kind":"def","line":124,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/ExtensionClass.lean#L124-L125","doc":"**Right splitting**: the projection admits a section. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.ExtensionClass.range_incl_eq_ker_proj","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.ExtensionClass.range_incl_eq_ker_proj","kind":"theorem","line":120,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/ExtensionClass.lean#L120-L122","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.ExtensionClass.SES.exact","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.ExtensionClass.SES.exact","kind":"theorem","line":116,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/ExtensionClass.lean#L116-L116","doc":"Exactness in the middle: `range incl = ker proj`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.ExtensionClass.SES.proj_surjective","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.ExtensionClass.SES.proj_surjective","kind":"theorem","line":114,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/ExtensionClass.lean#L114-L114","doc":"Exactness on the right. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.ExtensionClass.SES.incl_injective","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.ExtensionClass.SES.incl_injective","kind":"theorem","line":112,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/ExtensionClass.lean#L112-L112","doc":"Exactness on the left. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.ExtensionClass.SES.proj","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.ExtensionClass.SES.proj","kind":"def","line":110,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/ExtensionClass.lean#L110-L110","doc":"The projection to the quotient. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.ExtensionClass.SES.incl","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.ExtensionClass.SES.incl","kind":"def","line":108,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/ExtensionClass.lean#L108-L108","doc":"The inclusion of the sub-object. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.ExtensionClass.SES.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.ExtensionClass.SES.mk","kind":"ctor","line":104,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/ExtensionClass.lean#L104-L104","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.ExtensionClass.SES","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.ExtensionClass.SES","kind":"structure","line":99,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/ExtensionClass.lean#L99-L116","doc":"**A short exact sequence** `0 → C → B → A → 0` of `R`-modules.\n\nBundled because the splitting question is about the *sequence*, not about\nany one of its maps: `B` can be a direct sum in more than one way, and it is\nthe compatibility with `incl` and `proj` that an extension class records. ","signatureChunk":0}]}